The .glb files in this directory (ak47.glb, m4a1.glb, mp5.glb, awp.glb,
glock.glb) are from Tiny Strike (https://github.com/guyz/tinystrike), per that
project's own ASSETS.md: "The weapon and equipment GLBs in
assets/models/viewmodels/ ... were authored for Tiny Strike from the game's
original procedural weapon designs. They are released under the project's
ISC License."

npc-arms-ct.glb is also from Tiny Strike's assets/models/viewmodels/, but per
the same ASSETS.md it is itself a body-stripped derivative of
assets/models/soldier_ct.glb, which is derived from the Quaternius Toon
Shooter Game Kit (https://quaternius.com/packs/toonshootergamekit.html),
released by Quaternius under CC0 1.0 (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/).
Attribution is not required by CC0, but is included here with thanks to
Quaternius, consistent with Tiny Strike's own ASSETS.md.

